+## Wording checks
+
+A sentence in these files wraps across lines, so each check runs on text with newlines folded to
+spaces. Each check reads one section, so a phrase elsewhere in the file can't satisfy it. Define
+the section readers once per shell, from the worktree's root:
+
+```bash
+AP=claude/.claude/skills/approval-packet/SKILL.md
+AB=claude/.claude/skills/survey/writing/approval-brief.md
+CP=claude/.claude/skills/cairn-pass/SKILL.md
+UG=claude/.claude/docs/unattended-work-guards.md
+fold() { tr -s '\n' ' ' | tr -s ' '; }
+step2() { awk '/^2\. \*\*Write the fact file/{f=1} /^3\. \*\*Count the calls/{f=0} f' $AP | fold; }
+step8() { awk '/^8\. \*\*Read the notes/{f=1} /^9\. \*\*Clear the queue/{f=0} f' $AP | fold; }
+brief() { awk '/^## The packet writer.s brief/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' $AB; }
+block() { brief | awk '/^```text$/{f=1;next} /^```$/{f=0} f'; }
+contract() { awk '/^## The brief contract/{f=1;next} /^##+ /{f=0} f' $AB | fold; }
+packet() { awk '/^\*\*Packet\*\*/{f=1} f' $CP | fold; }
+usage() { awk 'tolower($0) ~ /^## .*usage/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' $UG | fold; }
+goal() { awk '/^## `\/goal`/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' $UG | fold; }
+```
+
+Each row's command is `<reader> | grep -c -F -- '<phrase>'`, with `-i` where the row says so. The
+"before" column is what the planner's run printed on 2026-11-12 at `99bbba1`. The executor's own
+before-run must print the same. A row whose before value already equals its after value is a kept
+phrase or an invariant, and the table marks it.
+
+Each phrase in the table is part of its task's outcome. The edit holds it exactly as the row
+writes it, backticks included: "never run `approval-queue merge`" matches, and "never runs" does
+not.
